  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Cloud shapes, the walls' streaks and sway, where rain, debris and leaves are caught and flung, the lightning's paths and the scar's grooves vary per cast. The 1 s brew, the touchdown at 1.0 s and the 2 s rage stay fixed so the warning ring is a fair telegraph."
  },
  "director_notes": "An original hurricane-scale storm, the big brother of the Tornado: where the tornado is a narrow funnel sent at one target, this one lands on an area and is wider than it is tall. Choices: (1) a full 1 s brew with a spinning warning_ring decal sized to the hit and a dark cloud deck gathering at sky height (smoke with wide spread_px), so the area attack is telegraphed; (2) touchdown on a lightning strike, a screen flash and a boom; (3) two vortex layers: a broad, flared eyewall (top radius 250 px, base 70 px: a calm eye) and a low, very wide, faint outer band (340 px) turning slower, so the storm reads wide from every view; (4) rain (droplet sparks), debris and leaves attached to the eyewall so they whip round in bands and are flung out when it collapses; (5) restriking lightning through the eye and a long shake; (6) the collapse narrows the eyewall, makes it snake and drops the outer band, with rolling dust and a vast swirl decal left behind; (7) sound: low rising wind → boom + thunder crack → roaring wind + rumble → dying wind."
}
